---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Features from '../components/Features.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';

const organizationJsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Organization',
  name: 'UnsaidSignals',
  url: 'https://unsaidsignals.com',
  logo: 'https://unsaidsignals.com/favicon.svg',
  sameAs: ['https://x.com', 'https://www.linkedin.com'],
};
---

<Page
  title="UnsaidSignals - Know what your team won't tell you | Anonymous team intelligence"
  description="Your team won't tell you what's really wrong. UnsaidSignals uses anonymous 2-minute pulses to surface hidden friction before people quit. Used by modern engineering leaders."
  canonical="/"
  jsonLd={organizationJsonLd}
>
  <Hero />
  
  <section id="example-insights" class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 lg:py-20">
    <div class="text-center">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-100 sm:text-3xl">What you'll discover about your team</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-zinc-400">Real insights from real teams (details anonymized)</p>
    </div>
    
    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="group relative overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-red-900/20 bg-gradient-to-br from-red-950/20 to-zinc-900">
        <div class="p-6">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-red-400">Critical Signal</p>
            <span class="text-xs text-zinc-500">This week</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="mt-3 text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-100">Trust erosion in backend team</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-300">
            3 of 5 engineers report feeling "out of the loop" on architectural decisions. 
            Pattern started after the new tech lead joined. Friction highest around code review process.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-4 rounded-lg bg-zinc-900/50 p-3">
            <p class="text-xs font-medium text-zinc-300">Suggested action:</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-zinc-400">Schedule architecture review meeting. Let team drive agenda. Address code review concerns directly.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      
      <div class="group relative overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-amber-900/20 bg-gradient-to-br from-amber-950/20 to-zinc-900">
        <div class="p-6">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-amber-400">Energy Shift</p>
            <span class="text-xs text-zinc-500">2 weeks trending</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="mt-3 text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-100">Sprint fatigue emerging</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-300">
            Team energy dropped 40% over last two sprints. Multiple mentions of "constant context switching" 
            and "too many parallel initiatives."
          </p>
          <div class="mt-4 rounded-lg bg-zinc-900/50 p-3">
            <p class="text-xs font-medium text-zinc-300">Suggested action:</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-zinc-400">Reduce WIP limits. Focus next sprint on completion over new starts. Consider a "cleanup sprint."</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      
      <div class="group relative overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-emerald-900/20 bg-gradient-to-br from-emerald-950/20 to-zinc-900">
        <div class="p-6">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-emerald-400">Positive Pattern</p>
            <span class="text-xs text-zinc-500">Building momentum</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="mt-3 text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-100">Cross-team collaboration improving</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-300">
            Frontend and design teams report 65% better alignment. New Friday sync meetings specifically 
            mentioned as "game changer."
          </p>
          <div class="mt-4 rounded-lg bg-zinc-900/50 p-3">
            <p class="text-xs font-medium text-zinc-300">Suggested action:</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-zinc-400">Protect this meeting. Share format with other teams. Celebrate the improvement publicly.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    
    <div class="mt-8 text-center">
      <p class="text-sm text-zinc-500">These insights come from 2-minute weekly pulses. Zero configuration required.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  
  <Features />

  <section id="how-it-works" class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 lg:py-20">
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-100">How it works</h2>
    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-3">
      <article class="rounded-xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-950/50 p-6">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-brand-300">Step 1</p>
        <h3 class="mt-3 text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-100">Weekly 2-minute pulse check</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-zinc-300">Short, anonymous responses make it safe for people to share what is actually happening.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-950/50 p-6">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-brand-300">Step 2</p>
        <h3 class="mt-3 text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-100">AI analyzes team patterns</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-zinc-300">Signals are clustered and interpreted to surface the patterns leaders cannot see in standups.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-950/50 p-6">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-brand-300">Step 3</p>
        <h3 class="mt-3 text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-100">Actionable narratives, not just numbers</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-zinc-300">You get weekly guidance with context and concrete actions for improving clarity, trust, and energy.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 lg:py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-zinc-100 sm:text-3xl">Built for psychological safety</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-zinc-400">Trust only exists when anonymity is guaranteed</p>
    </div>
    
    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/30 p-6">
        <div class="mb-3 flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-brand-500/10">
          <span class="text-lg">🔐</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-zinc-100">True anonymity</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-zinc-400">Responses are shuffled and aggregated. No tracking, no IP logging, no identifiers.</p>
      </div>
      
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/30 p-6">
        <div class="mb-3 flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-brand-500/10">
          <span class="text-lg">👥</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-zinc-100">5+ person minimum</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-zinc-400">Insights only generated for teams of 5+. Small team data is never exposed.</p>
      </div>
      
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/30 p-6">
        <div class="mb-3 flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-brand-500/10">
          <span class="text-lg">🚫</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-zinc-100">No individual data</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-zinc-400">Leaders see patterns and themes only. Individual responses are never accessible.</p>
      </div>
      
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/30 p-6">
        <div class="mb-3 flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-brand-500/10">
          <span class="text-lg">🏛️</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-zinc-100">SOC 2 compliant</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-zinc-400">Enterprise-grade security. Your team's trust is our foundation.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    
    <div class="mt-12 rounded-xl border border-brand-500/20 bg-brand-500/5 p-6 text-center">
      <p class="text-sm text-zinc-300">
        <span class="font-medium text-brand-300">Our promise:</span> We will never compromise anonymity for features. 
        If we can't do something while preserving complete anonymity, we won't do it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 lg:py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <h2 class="text-center text-2xl font-semibold text-zinc-100 sm:text-3xl">Common questions</h2>
      
      <div class="mt-10 space-y-6">
        <details class="group rounded-xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/30 p-6">
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-base font-semibold text-zinc-100">
            Will my team actually use this?
            <span class="ml-6 text-zinc-500 transition group-open:rotate-180">↓</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-zinc-400">
            Yes. 93% weekly participation rate across all teams. Why? It takes 2 minutes, it's truly anonymous, 
            and team members finally have a safe way to surface what's bothering them. They want to be heard.
          </p>
        </details>
        
        <details class="group rounded-xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/30 p-6">
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-base font-semibold text-zinc-100">
            How is this different from engagement surveys?
            <span class="ml-6 text-zinc-500 transition group-open:rotate-180">↓</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-zinc-400">
            Engagement surveys are quarterly autopsies. UnsaidSignals is a weekly heartbeat. 
            We focus on immediate, actionable patterns (not 50-page reports), and our AI surfaces 
            what matters now, not generic benchmarks from last quarter.
          </p>
        </details>
        
        <details class="group rounded-xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/30 p-6">
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-base font-semibold text-zinc-100">
            What if I discover something bad?
            <span class="ml-6 text-zinc-500 transition group-open:rotate-180">↓</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-zinc-400">
            You will. That's the point. Every team has hidden friction. The difference is whether you 
            find out early (when it's fixable) or late (when people quit). We provide specific actions 
            with every insight, so you're never left wondering "now what?"
          </p>
        </details>
        
        <details class="group rounded-xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/30 p-6">
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-base font-semibold text-zinc-100">
            How anonymous is "anonymous"?
            <span class="ml-6 text-zinc-500 transition group-open:rotate-180">↓</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-zinc-400">
            Completely. No IP tracking, no device IDs, no timing analysis. Responses are shuffled 
            before processing. We literally cannot tell who said what, even if we wanted to. 
            This isn't a feature—it's the foundation.
          </p>
        </details>
        
        <details class="group rounded-xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/30 p-6">
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-base font-semibold text-zinc-100">
            How long until I see results?
            <span class="ml-6 text-zinc-500 transition group-open:rotate-180">↓</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-zinc-400">
            First insights within 7 days of your team's first pulse. Most leaders report "aha moments" 
            in week 1, behavior changes by week 2, and measurable team improvement by week 4. 
            The earlier you start, the sooner you prevent problems.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTA />
</Page>
